No, it is only correct in one of the two charge storage modes. In the default mode it reads out of bounds.

## Why it is wrong

`getQView()` returns a view whose length depends on the container's storage mode (`src/PartBunch/ParticleContainer.hpp:130-135`). Its doc comment says: "In `SingleValue` mode this is a rank-1 view of length 1. In `Attributes` mode this is the per-particle attribute view."

- **Default is `SingleValue`**: `qmStorageMode_m = QMStorageMode::SingleValue`, and `QView_m` is commented as "Single shared scalar mode stored as a length-1 Kokkos view" (`ParticleContainer.hpp`, private members, around lines 959-971).
- **So `Qview(i)` is out of bounds for every `i > 0`** in that mode. Kokkos does not bounds-check in release builds, so this silently reads garbage.
- **The unit test confirms the length**: it asserts `qView.extent(0) == 1u` in `SingleValue` mode (`unit_tests/PartBunch/TestParticleContainer.cpp:103-126`).

## Fix

For this operation the container already has a member that does it correctly, so the simplest fix is to call it:

```cpp
pc->scaleDtByCharge();
```

`ParticleContainer::scaleDtByCharge()` (`ParticleContainer.hpp:582-601`) branches on the storage mode, uses `qView(i)` for `Attributes` and `QView(0)` for `SingleValue`, and ends with `Kokkos::fence()`. `unscaleDtByCharge()` at lines 610-629 is the inverse.

If you need the charge in your own kernel, use the pattern OPALX uses for mass in `src/Algorithms/DistributionMoments.cpp:48-87` (`massIsScalarView = (Mview.extent(0) == 1)`, then `massIsScalarView ? Mview(0) : Mview(k)`):

```cpp
auto Qview  = pc->getQView();
auto dtview = pc->dt.getView();

// SingleValue mode: length-1 view shared by all particles.
// Attributes mode: one entry per particle.
const bool chargeIsScalarView = (Qview.extent(0) == 1);

Kokkos::parallel_for(
        "scaleDtByCharge", pc->getLocalNum(),
        KOKKOS_LAMBDA(const size_t i) {
            dtview(i) *= chargeIsScalarView ? Qview(0) : Qview(i);
        });
Kokkos::fence();
```

The same applies to `getMView()` (`ParticleContainer.hpp:140-145`).

