Every element shares a block of common attributes (TYPE, APERTURE, L, ELEMEDGE, X, Y, Z,
the misalignments, ...). OpalElement declares their indices in an enum that ends in
COMMON and fills those slots of itsAttr in its own constructor. An element's enum
therefore has to continue at COMMON, and by convention its last entry is SIZE, which is
passed to the OpalElement constructor as the total number of attribute slots.

