examples.mcp_science_output:
**No.** On more than one MPI rank, this function counts only the lost particles on the rank that runs it, not the whole bunch.

**Why** (based on what the science MCP returned):

- `pc->getLocalNum()` is the number of particles on **this rank**. `InvalidMask` is a per-rank particle attribute, so the `Kokkos::parallel_reduce` only adds up the invalid flags of local particles. Kokkos reductions stay inside one process. You need an MPI reduction to get a total across ranks.
- OPALX does this two-step reduction itself in `ParticleContainer::deleteInvalidParticles()` (`src/PartBunch/ParticleContainer.hpp:909–954`, commit `32e8470`). It first counts locally with the same `parallel_reduce`, then runs `ippl::Comm->allreduce(localDestroyNum, globalDestroyNum, 1, std::plus<size_type>())`. Its doc comment (lines 895–908) says the return value is the "Global number of particles deleted (across all MPI ranks)".
- `PartBunch::gatherLoadBalanceStatistics()` (`src/PartBunch/PartBunch.cpp:300–304`) also builds global numbers from `getLocalNum()` with `ippl::Comm->allreduce(..., std::plus<size_t>())`.
- Your log line makes it worse. `*gmsg` normally prints from rank 0 only (I'm assuming this from how OPALX/IPPL `Inform` usually works; the MCP didn't confirm it). So "Lost N particles in total" would show rank 0's local count and label it as the total.

**Fixed version:**

```cpp
size_t MyCollimator::countLost(const std::shared_ptr<ParticleContainer_t>& pc) {
    const size_t nLocal = pc->getLocalNum();
    auto invalid        = pc->InvalidMask.getView();

    size_t localLost = 0;
    Kokkos::parallel_reduce(
            "MyCollimator::countLost", nLocal,
            KOKKOS_LAMBDA(const size_t i, size_t& count) { count += invalid(i) ? 1 : 0; },
            localLost);
    Kokkos::fence();

    // Sum over all MPI ranks; collective call, every rank must reach it.
    size_t globalLost = 0;
    ippl::Comm->allreduce(localLost, globalLost, 1, std::plus<size_t>());

    *gmsg << level2 << "Lost " << globalLost << " particles in total" << endl;
    return globalLost;
}
```

**Notes:**

- I used `allreduce` rather than `reduce` (which `AlpineManager::checkChargeConservation` in IPPL uses). With `allreduce`, every rank gets the same total, so any later decision based on the return value is consistent across ranks.
- Because `allreduce` is collective, every rank must call `countLost`, including ranks with zero local particles. Don't put the call behind a rank-local condition.
- If you're about to delete the particles anyway, you don't need a separate count: `pc->deleteInvalidParticles()` already returns the global number. Call `countLost` before the deletion, because `deleteInvalidParticles` resets `InvalidMask = false` afterwards (line ~944).

The MCP's index is at commits `32e8470`, `ca79921` and `f9d7679`, so line numbers may differ slightly from your checkout.

