No. That is the classic OPAL interface. In OPALX the bunch does not store particle
attributes.

PartBunch is a composition:
- one Cartesian domain, which owns the mesh and the field layout,
- one or more ParticleContainer objects, one per beam (species), which borrow that mesh
  and layout for their particle layout,
- a BunchStateHandler shared by the containers.
The attributes R, P, dt, E, B, Bin and InvalidMask are members of the container.
PartBunch::R(i) and P(i) exist only as stubs that throw an OpalException, and PartBunch
has no getTotalNum().

