The loop has three problems:

1. **`bunch->R(i)` throws on the first particle.** Positions are not stored on `PartBunch`. They are a particle attribute `R` on each particle container (`ParticleContainer_t = ParticleContainer<double, 3>`, see `src/PartBunch/PartBunchFwd.h`). You reach a container through `bunch->getParticleContainer(i)`.
2. **The attribute lives in device memory (Kokkos).** You can't index it on the host directly. Make a host mirror of `pc->R.getView()` and `deep_copy` into it. OPALX does this itself in `H5PartWrapperForPT::writeStepData` (`src/Structure/H5PartWrapperForPT.cpp` lines 429–448). The tests do the same, for example `unit_tests/AbsBeamline/TestMarkOutsideAperture.cpp` lines 190–196:
   ```cpp
