   Kokkos::deep_copy(R_host, pc->R.getView());
   for (size_t i = 0; i < pc->getLocalNum(); ++i) { ... R_host(i)[0] ... }
   ```
3. **Wrong loop bound.** Each MPI rank holds only its local particles, so loop to `pc->getLocalNum()`, as `writeStepData` does (line 431). `getTotalNum()` is the global count. `PartBunch::getTotalNumAllContainers()` (PartBunch.h 232–240) adds `pc->getTotalNum()` over all containers. Looping to a global count on one rank goes past the end of the local data.

A bunch can also hold several particle containers, and some can be inactive or null. `ParallelTracker::resetFields` (`src/Algorithms/ParallelTracker.cpp` 1112–1125) and `updateReferenceParticles` (1423–1472) loop over them with `getNumParticleContainers()`, `isPcActive(i)` and a null check.

### Fixed version

```cpp
#include <Kokkos_Core.hpp>
#include "PartBunch/PartBunch.h"

void MyDiagnostic::record(PartBunch_t* bunch) {
    const size_t nContainers = bunch->getNumParticleContainers();
    for (size_t c = 0; c < nContainers; ++c) {
        if (!bunch->isPcActive(c)) {
            continue;
        }
        auto pc = bunch->getParticleContainer(c);
        if (!pc) {
            continue;
        }

        // Copy the device-side position attribute into a host mirror.
        auto rDevice = pc->R.getView();
        auto rHost   = Kokkos::create_mirror_view(rDevice);
        Kokkos::fence();
        Kokkos::deep_copy(rHost, rDevice);

        // Only the particles owned by this rank.
        const size_t nLocal = pc->getLocalNum();
        for (size_t i = 0; i < nLocal; ++i) {
            const Vector_t<double, 3> r = rHost(i);
            addSample(r);
        }
    }
}
```

If you only care about the first container (the single-species case), use `auto pc = bunch->getParticleContainer();` with no argument, as in `writeStepData` line 503 and the `makeBunch` helper in `unit_tests/AbsBeamline/TestMultipoleTCurvedConstRadius.cpp` line 207.

- **Getting all samples on one rank:** each rank only sees its own particles. To collect every sample in one place, gather them across ranks yourself, for example with MPI or `ippl::Comm`.
- **Units:** `ParticleContainer.hpp` has `switchToUnitlessPositions`/`switchOffUnitlessPositions`. If your diagnostic runs inside the tracking step, check which representation `R` is in at that point.

One gap: the science MCP lookup for whether `PartBunch` itself declares `getTotalNum()` or `getLocalNum()` returned nothing, and a follow-up query failed with an HTTP 502. So I don't recommend calling either on the bunch. The code above only calls them on a particle container, where the source above uses them.

